# tv_menu_headless: the TV in-game menu and its input ownership, through the real App (headless, no ImGui).
# Run with:  virtualjaguar --headless --frames 30 --tv-test-script tv_menu_headless.txt
# (VJ_LIBRASHADER must point at a missing path when this script is run by hand, as cmake/VJTvTests.cmake sets it for ctest: a
# shader runtime would add a Picture row and the Down counts below would be off.)
# One event per line:  <ms> <verb> <args>.  <ms> is a script time; the gap to the previous line is the least real time
# that passes between the two (the hold arbiter reads the real clock).  Lines starting with # are comments.
#   load PATH            drop PATH on the window (the normal drop route)
#   key down|up|tap NAME a key event (SDL scancode name: F4, Escape, F8; "ctrl+L", "ctrl+shift+T" = with those held)
#   pad down|up|tap BTN  a button on the runner's virtual gamepad (SDL button name: a, b, dpdown, misc1)
#   mouse X Y           move the pointer to X,Y in the main window: a MOUSE_MOTION with the travel since the last `mouse` line as xrel / yrel
#                       (windowed: the real pointer is warped there too, for hover tests; headless: only the event)
#   expect fullscreen=0|1 menu-pinned=0|1 menu-visible=0|1 (menu-visible needs a windowed rendered frame)
#   focus lost|gained    the window loses / gets keyboard focus
#   typing on|off        pretend a text box has focus (input.uiWantsKeyboard)
#   capture help|tvmenu  begin binding that action on the keyboard (the next key becomes its binding)
#   capture nav:INTENT   begin rebinding a menu button of the virtual pad (confirm back menu favorite start tabprev tabnext pageprev
#                        pagenext search): the next pad button becomes it (#1021).  expect cfg=...{padguid}... is its GUID.
#   tvsetting off|manual|auto  set the stored TV-mode setting and reconfigure (as Settings will); off = never, auto = also in fullscreen and on a pad press
#   fullscreen on|off    enter / leave fullscreen (headless: the flag and the edge TV mode is told about, no window)
#   hintreset            forget the one-time TV mode hint (ui.tv_hint_shown and this run's flag) and zero toast-count
#   expect toast=TEXT    the text of the last toast (the rest of the line, spaces included);  expect toast-count=N  toasts shown since start
#   expect tv-setting=off|manual|auto  the stored setting (a fresh config takes the build default: auto on a CTest build)
#   navdefault INTENT    the Default button of that menu intent of the virtual pad (back to the family's button, partner swapped back)
#   command settings|bios|library|tvmode  what the native macOS menu / tray click runs (App::runNativeCommand); a synthesized ctrl+, is
#                        ignored in a real window, so this is the Mac path
#   settings-group KEY   the TV Settings rail opens on that group next (the shell's focus memory "settings/rail": picture sound interface library
#                        achievements discord neuro, or core:<category key>, e.g. core:video); the rail's length varies with the build and the session
#   hardcore-pause deny|allow  allowPause() refuses (as hardcore does between pauses) / allows; the in-game menu then opens without pausing
#   expect menu-owns-input=0|1  the in-game menu has the pads (open: paused, netplay or hardcore running on)
#   expect menu-slot=ID|none  the screen in the in-game menu's slot (settings, overlays, achievements, library)
#   expect menu-page=root|save|load|confirm-reset|confirm-close|confirm-launch  the in-game menu's page
#   expect menu-open=0|1  paused=0|1  loaded=0|1  capturing=0|1  fast-forward=0|1  core-input=0|1  kb-bind=help|tvmenu:KEY
#   expect tv=0|1         TV mode is on
#   expect tv-screen=ID   the id of the TV screen on top (home, library, ...)
#   expect tv-focus=LABEL the label of what has the focus on the top TV screen (Settings: the group on the rail, or the row in its list;
#                         the rest of the line, spaces included); Screen::focusLabel().  With the in-game menu open: the slot screen's, else the menu row's
#   expect tv-group=KEY   the key of the group on the TV Settings rail (picture sound interface library ... core:video); Screen::focusGroup()
#   expect tv-owns-input=0|1  the TV shell has the pads and keys (0 while a desktop window covers the TV screens)
#   expect settings-open=0|1  the desktop Settings window is open
#   expect tv-more=0|1        it was opened by "More settings..." in TV mode: the pads and the arrow keys are its own (tv_more_settings.h)
#   expect home-visible=0|1   the desktop library is standing in for the game (never while TV mode is on)
#   expect library-window=0|1 the desktop Game library window is open
#   expect desk-pad=0|1       the desktop library owns the pads (#1021): TV off, no game running, no capture / desktop window, no mouse-opened popup
#                             (headless has no ImGui context, so that last part is covered by tv_ui_smoke)
#   axis NAME VALUE       set an axis of the virtual pad (SDL axis name: righty, lefttrigger; -32768..32767)
#   expect desk-scroll=0|1    the desktop nav holds a right-stick scroll (nonzero)
#   expect desk-pending=N     commands the desktop nav has queued (headless nothing draws the library, so they stay queued)
#   expect desk-popup=0|1     a library popup (tile menu, BIOS popup) opened from the pad is open and driven by it
#   saveconfig           App::saveConfig() (a headless run keeps its config in a private temp dir)
#   expect cfg=KEY:VALUE  the config holds KEY = VALUE; KEY:absent = the config has no such key
#   expect core-option=KEY:VALUE  the core option KEY reads VALUE (a session override, else the saved value: CoreHost::optionValueFor)
#   wait library         WINDOWED ONLY: block the script until the Library has scanned (not scanning, and at least one
#                        game); FAIL after 120 s.  The gaps of the lines after it count from the moment it is released.
#   shot PATH            WINDOWED ONLY: save the window as a PNG at the end of the next UI frame (that frame's TV drawing
#                        included).  Leave a gap before it for a screen change to finish animating.
#   quit                 WINDOWED ONLY: end the run through the normal teardown
#   (headless, wait / shot / quit fail their line with "windowed only": the Library is scanned by threads that only a
#   windowed run starts, and there is no window to save.  Windowed, any FAIL is printed and the script goes on.)
#   (core-input=1: the core would read some Player 1 pad button right now; the expect takes the snapshot itself)
# An expect first lets the per-frame input housekeeping run, so a fired hold has been handled by then.

# TV mode with no game (Manual): F4 turns it on and off; Esc at the root is not the shell's; Off ignores F4; the toggle works under
# Auto too; a Share hold toggles it too.  (A fresh config takes the build default, Auto on a CTest build: start from Manual.)
0     tvsetting manual
0     expect loaded=0
0     expect tv=0
0     key tap F4
40    expect tv=1
40    expect tv-screen=home
60    key tap Escape          # at root: not the shell's
100   expect tv=1
100   key tap F4
140   expect tv=0
140   tvsetting off
160   key tap F4
200   expect tv=0
200   tvsetting auto           # the toggle works under Auto too
220   key tap F4
260   expect tv=1
260   key tap F4
300   expect tv=0
300   tvsetting manual
320   pad down misc1
920   pad up misc1
960   expect tv=1
960   key tap F4
1000  expect tv=0

# saveConfig() never writes ui.tv_mode (a stored value would pin a default that moves between builds); only a change in Settings
# does.  The remembered on/off state (ui.tv_manual_on) is written under Manual.  Whatever the setting, the key stays out of the config.
1000  tvsetting manual
1000  saveconfig
1000  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1000  key tap F4
1040  expect tv=1
1040  saveconfig
1040  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1040  expect cfg=ui.tv_manual_on:1
1040  key tap F4
1080  expect tv=0
1080  saveconfig
1080  expect cfg=ui.tv_manual_on:0
1080  tvsetting auto
1080  saveconfig
1080  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1080  tvsetting manual

# With TV mode on, Ctrl+L (File > Game library) is the TV Library, never the desktop library window (#991): the Library section, again
# changes nothing, B goes Home.  With it off the home library is showing, so Ctrl+L only focuses its search box.  (The window the key
# used to open is still reachable with `--show-window library`, a dev flag, not a user path.)
1080  expect home-visible=1
1080  key tap ctrl+L
1120  expect library-window=0
1120  key tap F4
1160  expect tv=1
1160  expect home-visible=0
1160  expect tv-owns-input=1
1160  expect tv-screen=home
1160  key tap ctrl+L
1200  expect library-window=0
1200  expect tv-screen=library
1200  expect tv-owns-input=1
1200  key tap ctrl+L
1240  expect library-window=0
1240  expect tv-screen=library
1240  expect tv-owns-input=1
1240  pad tap b
1280  expect tv-screen=home
1280  pad tap rightshoulder
1320  expect tv-screen=library
1320  pad tap leftshoulder
1360  expect tv-screen=home
1360  key tap F4
1400  expect tv=0

# "Desktop settings..." from TV mode (#991): A on the last row of Interface opens the desktop Settings window and hands it the pad.
# RB x3 reaches Settings (Home, Library, Achievements, Settings).  The rail is the app's tabs, then the core's categories (read at startup,
# so they are there with no game): Picture, Sound, Interface, ... (Down x2); Right enters the list, whose last row is Desktop settings...
# whatever else the build adds above it (Down x20 clamps there).
# While the window is open the shell has stepped aside (tv-owns-input=0) and the pad is the window's: a shoulder button that
# would change section does nothing, and B closes it (no popup, no active item), giving the pad back.
1400  key tap F4
1440  expect tv=1
1440  pad tap rightshoulder
1460  pad tap rightshoulder
1480  pad tap rightshoulder
1500  expect tv-screen=settings
# TV Settings, long lists (#991 Task 20), with no game loaded: the rail opens on Picture; Down x3 is Library (Picture, Sound, Interface, Library:
# the app's own groups come first and are in every build).  Achievements, Discord and Neuro are gated on the build and the session, so
# the walk to the core's Video category uses the shell's memory (settings-group) instead of counting them.  In Video the third row is
# the internal resolution: Right steps it with NO game (the core options are read at startup), the value is the core's, and it is saved
# as opt.<key> for the next game, and STAYS 2x: the first `load` below reads it back, and the in-menu change at the end steps it down.
# Back and the memory put the rail on Picture again, so the walk below is unchanged.
1500  expect tv-group=picture
1500  pad tap dpdown
1510  pad tap dpdown
1520  pad tap dpdown
1560  expect tv-group=library
1560  settings-group core:video
1570  expect tv-group=core:video
1570  pad tap dpright          # into the list, on its first row
1580  pad tap dpdown
1590  pad tap dpdown
1630  expect tv-focus=Internal Resolution (Restart Required)
1630  pad tap dpright          # 1x -> 2x
1670  expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:2x
1670  saveconfig
1670  expect cfg=opt.virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:2x
1710  pad tap dpup               # the group remembers its row: back to the first, the later in-menu walk starts there
1720  pad tap dpup
1730  pad tap b                # the list -> the rail
1740  settings-group picture
1750  expect tv-group=picture
1760  pad tap dpdown
1770  pad tap dpdown
1790  pad tap dpright
1810  pad tap dpdown
1820  pad tap dpdown
1830  pad tap dpdown
1840  pad tap dpdown
1850  pad tap dpdown
1860  pad tap dpdown
1870  pad tap dpdown
1880  pad tap dpdown
1890  pad tap dpdown
1900  pad tap dpdown
1910  pad tap dpdown
1920  pad tap dpdown
1930  pad tap dpdown
1940  pad tap dpdown
1950  pad tap dpdown
1960  pad tap dpdown
1970  pad tap dpdown
1980  pad tap dpdown
1990  pad tap dpdown
2000  pad tap dpdown
2020  pad tap a
2060  expect settings-open=1
2060  expect tv-more=1
2060  expect tv-owns-input=0
2060  pad tap dpdown              # the window's, not the shell's
2080  pad tap leftshoulder        # would step back to Achievements
2100  expect tv-screen=settings
2100  pad tap b
2140  expect settings-open=0
2140  expect tv-more=0
2140  expect tv-owns-input=1
# Esc closes it too (the focus is still on More settings...), and so does Ctrl+, -- which also ends the TV hand-off.  The next
# Ctrl+, is the TV Settings screen, never the plain desktop window (#991): already there it changes nothing, from another section it
# switches to Settings.
2140  pad tap a
2180  expect tv-more=1
2180  key tap Escape
2220  expect settings-open=0
2220  expect tv-more=0
2220  pad tap a
2260  expect tv-more=1
2260  key tap ctrl+,
2300  expect settings-open=0
2300  expect tv-more=0
2300  key tap ctrl+,
2340  expect settings-open=0
2340  expect tv-screen=settings
2340  expect tv-more=0
2340  pad tap leftshoulder
2350  expect tv-screen=achievements
2350  key tap ctrl+,
2380  expect tv-screen=settings
2380  expect settings-open=0
# The native macOS menu / tray runs Cmd::Settings, not a key (a synthesized Ctrl+, is ignored in a real window): the same.
2380  pad tap leftshoulder
2385  expect tv-screen=achievements
2385  command settings
2390  expect tv-screen=settings
2390  expect settings-open=0
2390  pad tap leftshoulder        # back to Home (the shell remembers the section across TV mode off / on)
2400  pad tap leftshoulder
2410  pad tap leftshoulder
2420  expect tv-screen=home
2420  key tap F4
2460  expect tv=0

# Desktop pad navigation (#1021): the desktop library owns the pads while TV mode is off, no game is running and the home
# library shows.  A shoulder button is a mapped intent (SectionNext = next tab) and queues a command; TV mode on (or an edge of
# any ownership input) hands the pad to the TV screens and clears what was queued.
2460  expect desk-pad=1
2460  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:absent
2460  expect toast-count=0
2460  pad tap rightshoulder
# The first consumed press under Manual shows the one-time hint (6 s toast, wording from the pad's own TV-menu binding: the virtual
# pad has Share, so its default is the Share hold), stored before it shows; a second press shows nothing more.
2500  expect toast=Press Share (hold) or F4 for TV mode
2500  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:1
2500  expect toast-count=1
2500  expect desk-pending=1
2500  pad tap leftshoulder
2540  expect toast-count=1
2540  expect desk-pending=2
2540  key tap F4
2580  expect tv=1
2580  expect desk-pad=0
2580  expect desk-pending=0      # the edge cleared the queue
2580  pad tap leftshoulder        # TV's, not the desktop library's: nothing queues
2620  expect desk-pending=0
2620  key tap F4
2660  expect tv=0
2660  expect desk-pad=1
# A binding capture owns the pad.
2660  capture help
2700  expect capturing=1
2700  expect desk-pad=0
2700  key tap Return             # ends the capture
2740  expect capturing=0
2740  expect desk-pad=1
# Start (Menu) is not the library's: it stays the app's and queues nothing.
2740  pad tap start
2780  expect desk-pending=0

# A right stick pushed while the library listens is a scroll; losing the pad (a desktop window opens, Settings here) or the
# window's focus zeroes it, so a stick let go meanwhile cannot scroll on.  Settings takes the pad while open.
2820  axis righty 30000
2860  expect desk-scroll=1
2860  key tap ctrl+,
2900  expect desk-pad=0
2900  expect desk-scroll=0
2900  axis righty 0
2940  key tap ctrl+,
2980  expect desk-pad=1
2980  expect desk-scroll=0
2980  axis righty 30000
3020  expect desk-scroll=1
3020  focus lost
3060  expect desk-scroll=0
3060  axis righty 0
3100  expect desk-scroll=0

# Auto (#991 phase 4): a mapped pad press in the desktop library turns TV mode on and is consumed (nothing queued, nothing
# launched); a printable key turns a controller-started TV mode off; fullscreen holds it; leaving fullscreen ends it.
3140  tvsetting auto
3140  expect tv=0
3140  expect desk-pad=1
3140  pad tap a
3180  expect tv=1
3180  expect tv-screen=home
3180  expect loaded=0
3180  expect desk-pending=0
3180  expect toast-count=1            # no second hint (and the switching press takes the return before the hint site)
3180  key tap Escape               # approval C: Esc, Enter and shortcuts are not "typing": a controller-started TV mode stays on
3180  expect tv=1
3180  key tap Return
3180  expect tv=1
3180  key tap ctrl+H               # a printable key with Ctrl held is a shortcut
3180  expect tv=1
3180  key tap H
3220  expect tv=0
3220  pad tap dpdown
3260  expect tv=1
3260  fullscreen on
3280  expect fullscreen=1
3280  key tap H
3320  expect tv=1                 # fullscreen holds it
3320  fullscreen off
3360  expect tv=0
3360  fullscreen on
3400  expect tv=1                 # the fullscreen trigger on its own
3400  key tap ctrl+shift+T
3440  expect tv=0                 # manual wins ...
3440  key tap H
3480  expect tv=0
3480  fullscreen off
3480  fullscreen on
3520  expect tv=1                 # ... until the next edge
3520  fullscreen off
3560  expect tv=0
3560  pad tap touchpad            # no nav intent (C_HELP's button): not a trigger.  (Not misc1: a Share tap opens the keypad overlay)
3600  expect tv=0
3600  pad tap start
3640  expect tv=1                 # Start is a mapped intent: it switches
3640  key tap H
3680  expect tv=0
3680  key tap ctrl+,              # a desktop window takes the pad before the trigger sees it
3720  pad tap dpdown
3760  expect tv=0
3760  key tap ctrl+,
# A Share hold toggles TV mode (Manual cause) and is not also the controller trigger (it would switch on at the press, off at the hold).
3760  pad down misc1
4380  expect tv=1
4380  pad up misc1
4420  expect tv=1
4420  key tap F4
4460  expect tv=0
4460  tvsetting manual
4460  saveconfig
4460  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent

# The Auto rows in TV Settings (#991 phase 4): they exist only under Auto, a change is stored and keeps TV mode on (a reconfigure
# makes it a Manual-started one), and Auto -> Manual removes them.  Every step of the walk is anchored by `expect tv-focus=` (the
# group on the rail, the row in the list), because the shell remembers Settings across TV mode off and on and the Base layer resumes
# the level (list or rail) and the row it was left on: nothing here may assume where an earlier test stopped.  TV mode comes back on
# at Home.  RB x3 opens Settings at whatever level it was left; one Back then goes from the list to the groups, or from the groups
# to Home; LB x3 makes it Home either way, leaving the memory on the groups; RB x3 reopens Settings there.  Up x4 must read Picture
# and Down x2 Interface; only then does Right enter the list (on the groups it only enters, it changes nothing).  Up x8 clamps to
# Show FPS, Down x4 must read Auto: in fullscreen, and only then do Left / Right change a value.
# With Auto on the list starts Show FPS, Show the controls overlay, Theme, TV mode, Auto: in fullscreen, Auto: when a controller is used,
# ... and ends with Desktop settings... (Down x20 clamps there).
4460  tvsetting auto
4470  key tap F4
4510  expect tv=1
4510  expect tv-screen=home
4520  pad tap rightshoulder
4530  pad tap rightshoulder
4540  pad tap rightshoulder
4580  expect tv-screen=settings
4590  pad tap b
4600  pad tap leftshoulder
4610  pad tap leftshoulder
4620  pad tap leftshoulder
4660  expect tv-screen=home
4670  pad tap rightshoulder
4680  pad tap rightshoulder
4690  pad tap rightshoulder
4730  expect tv-screen=settings
4740  pad tap dpup
4750  pad tap dpup
4760  pad tap dpup
4770  pad tap dpup
4810  expect tv-focus=Picture
4820  pad tap dpdown
4830  pad tap dpdown
4880  expect tv-focus=Interface
4890  pad tap dpright
4900  pad tap dpup
4910  pad tap dpup
4920  pad tap dpup
4930  pad tap dpup
4940  pad tap dpup
4950  pad tap dpup
4960  pad tap dpup
4970  pad tap dpup
4980  pad tap dpup
4990  pad tap dpup
5000  pad tap dpup
5010  pad tap dpup
5020  pad tap dpup
5030  pad tap dpup
5040  pad tap dpup
5050  pad tap dpup
5060  pad tap dpup
5070  pad tap dpup
5080  pad tap dpup
5090  pad tap dpup
5130  expect tv-focus=Show FPS
5140  pad tap dpdown
5150  pad tap dpdown
5160  pad tap dpdown
5170  pad tap dpdown
5210  expect tv-focus=Auto: in fullscreen
5210  pad tap dpleft
5250  expect cfg=ui.tv_auto_fullscreen:0
5250  expect tv=1   # still on (Manual cause after the reconfigure)
5260  pad tap dpright
5300  expect cfg=ui.tv_auto_fullscreen:1
5300  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent   # the checkbox change saved the config, and still did not pin the default
5310  pad tap dpup
5350  expect tv-focus=TV mode
5350  pad tap dpleft   # Auto -> Manual
5390  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:manual
5390  expect tv=1
5400  pad tap dpdown
5410  pad tap dpdown
5420  pad tap dpdown
5430  pad tap dpdown
5440  pad tap dpdown
5450  pad tap dpdown
5460  pad tap dpdown
5470  pad tap dpdown
5480  pad tap dpdown
5490  pad tap dpdown
5500  pad tap dpdown
5510  pad tap dpdown
5520  pad tap dpdown
5530  pad tap dpdown
5540  pad tap dpdown
5550  pad tap dpdown
5560  pad tap dpdown
5570  pad tap dpdown
5580  pad tap dpdown
5590  pad tap dpdown
5630  expect tv-focus=Desktop settings…   # the Auto rows are gone
5630  pad tap a
5670  expect tv-more=1
5670  pad tap b
5710  expect tv-more=0
5720  pad tap leftshoulder   # back to Home: the shell resumes the screen TV mode was left on, and the lines below start from Home
5730  pad tap leftshoulder
5740  pad tap leftshoulder
5780  expect tv-screen=home
5780  key tap F4
5820  expect tv=0

# The hint never shows under Off or Auto, even with the key unset and the run's flag clear (hintreset: forget both, zero toast-count).
5820  hintreset
5820  tvsetting off
5820  expect desk-pad=1
5820  expect desk-pending=0
5830  pad tap rightshoulder
5850  expect desk-pending=1            # the desktop library took the press (so the hint site was reached) ...
5850  expect toast-count=0             # ... and showed nothing
5850  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:absent
5850  tvsetting auto
5850  mouse 100 100                  # (TV mode is off: the pointer's start is not travel)
5860  pad tap a                      # Auto's switching press: consumed, no hint
5870  expect tv=1
5870  expect toast-count=0
5870  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:absent
# The mouse path through App::handleEvent: 30 px of motion (3 x 10) leave a controller-started TV mode on, the 4th step (40 px) ends it.
# (A warp reports xrel = 0, so `mouse` also pushes the motion event itself; the windowed check on the Studio sends the same.)
5870  mouse 110 100
5870  mouse 120 100
5870  mouse 130 100
5875  expect tv=1
5875  mouse 140 100
5880  expect tv=0

# A game to play with.
5880  load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
5920  expect loaded=1
5920  expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:2x      # the TV Settings change made with no game (first block above) reached this one

# Auto with a game running (#991 phase 4): a pad press is the game's, never a trigger; fullscreen still turns TV mode on and leaves
# the game running, unpaused, with its input; leaving fullscreen turns it off.
5920  tvsetting auto
5920  pad tap dpdown
5960  expect tv=0                 # the game owns the pad
5960  fullscreen on
6000  expect tv=1
6000  expect menu-open=0
6000  expect paused=0
6000  pad down dpright
6040  expect core-input=1
6040  pad up dpright
6040  fullscreen off
6080  expect tv=0
6080  tvsetting manual

# F4 opens the menu (and pauses the game), F4 again closes it.
6120   key tap F4
6160   expect menu-open=1
6160   expect paused=1
6180   key tap F4
6220   expect menu-open=0
6220   expect paused=0

# A pause the player made is theirs: the menu does not undo it.
6240   key tap F8
6260   expect paused=1
6280   key tap F4
6320   expect menu-open=1
6340   key tap F4
6380   expect menu-open=0
6380   expect paused=1
6400   key tap F8
6420   expect paused=0

# F4 while a text box has the keyboard does nothing.
6440   typing on
6460   key tap F4
6500   expect menu-open=0
6500   typing off

# Esc is Back, and Back on the menu's first page is Resume.
6520   key tap F4
6560   expect menu-open=1
6580   key tap Escape
6620   expect menu-open=0
6620   expect paused=0

# A key let go while the menu is open still reaches the app (Tab is fast-forward and has to be let go of).
6640   key down Tab
6660   expect fast-forward=1
6680   key tap F4
6720   expect menu-open=1
6740   key up Tab
6780   expect fast-forward=0
6800   key tap F4
6840   expect menu-open=0

# A Share tap is not a hold: no menu.
# (`pad tap` presses and releases inside one line, so a stalled runner cannot stretch it into a hold.)
6880   pad tap misc1
6960   expect menu-open=0

# A Share hold of 600 ms opens the menu; letting go leaves it open.
6980   pad down misc1
7600  expect menu-open=1
7600  expect paused=1
7620  pad up misc1
7660  expect menu-open=1

# A Share hold while it is open closes it (the edge reaches the arbiter before the shell).
7680  pad down misc1
8320  expect menu-open=0
8320  expect paused=0
