# Menu buttons (#1021): Set captures the virtual pad's next button for a menu intent, and writes no game binding.  North (Y)
# becomes Confirm; Y was Favorite's, so the two swap (Favorite takes Confirm's old button, South).
12060  expect capturing=0
12060  capture nav:confirm
12100  expect capturing=1
12100  pad tap y
12140  expect capturing=0
12140  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:by
12140  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:ba
# Default on one half of the swap puts both back: no two intents on one button, and no stray key.
12140  navdefault confirm
12180  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:absent
12180  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:absent
# A reserved button is refused and writes nothing: the D-pad moves, so it cannot be a menu button.
12180  capture nav:back
12220  pad tap dpup
12260  expect capturing=0
12260  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# So is the button that opens the controls overlay (the pad's C_HELP, the touchpad button), as the TV-menu button is.
12260  capture nav:back
12300  pad tap touchpad
12340  expect capturing=0
12340  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# Esc cancels a menu-button capture without writing anything.
12340  capture nav:search
12380  key tap Escape
12420  expect capturing=0
12420  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.search:absent

# A core option changed inside the in-game menu reaches the core once the menu is closed.  Down x6 from Resume is Settings (Save state,
# Load state, Library, Achievements, Overlays, Settings), A opens the screen (the groups, on Video: `settings-group` puts the shell's memory
# there, so no count of rail items is needed), A opens Video (the core's category of that name: it is a TV Settings group like the app's),
# Down x2 is Internal resolution (Fast blitter, True color, then it), Left steps it from 2x (the first TV Settings walk set it with no game) to 1x; B x3 is rows -> groups -> the menu -> Resume.  The write is a posted command: the value is read after the menu
# has closed and the paused core has had its boundary.
12460   load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
12500   expect loaded=1
12500   expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:2x      # (set by the first TV Settings walk, with no game)
12500   settings-group core:video
